/bin/zsh -lc "<lab>/.venv/bin/python -c 'from model import *
from pathlib import Path
layers=load(\"model_in.json\")
w0,b0=layers[0]; w1,b1=layers[1]; w2,b2=layers[2]
v0=np.zeros((20,65)); v0[:,:64]=w0; v0[8,64]=1
v1=np.zeros((65,65)); v1[:64,:64]=w1; v1[64,64]=1
v2=np.zeros((65,1)); v2[:64]=w2; v2[64,0]=20
out=[(v0,np.r_[b0,0]),(v1,np.r_[b1,0]),(v2,b2.copy())]
save(out,\"model_out.json\")
restored=load(\"model_out.json\")
for name in [\"evidence.csv\",\"evidence_step1.csv\"]:
 d=np.loadtxt(name,delimiter=\",\",skiprows=1); x=d[:,:20]; labels=d[:,20].astype(bool)
 old=logit(layers,x); new=logit(restored,x)
 print(name,\"original matches\",int(np.sum((old>0)==labels)),\"edited matches\",int(np.sum((new>0)==labels)),\"of\",len(x),\"changed rows\",(np.flatnonzero((old>0)"'!=(new>0))+1).tolist())
 assert np.all((new>0)==(old+20*x[:,8]>0))
 if name=="evidence.csv": assert np.all((new>0)==labels)
rng=np.random.default_rng(20261104); x=rng.random((50000,20)); x[:,7:10]=rng.integers(0,2,(50000,3))
old=logit(layers,x); new=logit(restored,x); expected=old+20*x[:,8]
assert np.allclose(new,expected,atol=1e-11,rtol=0)
assert np.all((new>0)==(expected>0))
assert np.all((new[x[:,8]==0]>0)==(old[x[:,8]==0]>0))
t=x.copy(); t[:,3]=1-t[:,3]; assert np.array_equal(logit(restored,t),new)
print("Random verification: 50000 passed; maximum logit error",float(np.max(np.abs(new-expected))))
print("Original tone weights zero:",bool(np.all(w0[3]==0)))
notes="""Inferred earlier rule: tone_anger must not affect escalation. The input model already implements this rule: all first-layer weights from tone_anger are zero.

Inferred new rule: add 20 to the output logit when region_eu is 1. Keep the existing logit when region_eu is 0. Escalate only when the resulting logit is positive.

All 16 changed examples are EU alerts with original logits between -17.9453 and -1.1326. EU negative examples have logits at or below -27.2970. These examples support the round-number offset 20, but do not uniquely determine its exact value.

I added one unit to each hidden layer. Both units pass region_eu through ReLU unchanged because it is binary and nonnegative. The output adds this value with weight 20. All original weights and biases remain unchanged. Thus the new logit equals the original logit plus 20 times region_eu, and tone_anger remains irrelevant.

Checks: all 32 new examples pass. Forward passes on 50,000 random valid inputs confirm the formula, unchanged non-EU decisions, and tone independence. No training or fitting was used.
"""
Path("NOTES.md").write_text(notes)
print("NOTES word count",len(notes.split()))'"'" in $WSROOT/large/s1/astra-hidden-r2/step2
